 version, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n3. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A status check afterward shows the service healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It says what failed, why I picked v2.3.0, the result of the rollback, and that the v2.3.1 problem needs a root cause before it's redeployed. The first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterward, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The list now shows only INC-0001, so there's no duplicate.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BE9D5k2Te8HNCXgQY3vNaB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VbLimx7y4ycqZgKKcZWJYk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01N4xGicu964Jy1CpeM9GUje", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q4mDZ3V7quj3tKyQzFSDi4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KfDYu1qzuNRyBt4eWHWqUZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01K6SBDNUdJrTjQ6zVGR18qR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01VrwLKLRKdE71r3q43oQc3N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "No incident was created, so I'll retry with the same idempotency key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01VkbiXgZwMz2gzJYLRuJbPb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy, checkout-api v2.3.1 failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. The deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions. After the rollback the service reports healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XMx323msFezvf7qum6iWEV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n1. **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with an error rate of about 18%.\n2. **Choosing the version:** The deploy history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc as unhealthy. v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. It's an earlier healthy version, so no change-manager approval was needed.\n3. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A status check afterward shows the service healthy, with an error rate of about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged on-call. It says what failed, why I picked v2.3.0, the result of the rollback, and that the v2.3.1 problem needs a root cause before it's redeployed. The first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterward, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The list now shows only INC-0001, so there's no duplicate.", "type": "text"}]}]}